"Doug Freyburger" <dfreybur@yahoo.com> wrote:
>The Staff of Misspellllling does both double damage and level
>drain.  So when faced with monsters that don't resist level
>drain I'm not convinced.

Your brain has clearly dropped every discussion about the player's
to-hit bonus in the past couple of years in the circular file, then.

With Strength 18/**, Dex 18, and 14th level, you get +20 to hit.  Maxed
luck takes that to +33, +6 for a lightly-maxed weapon takes it to +39.
The to-hit penalty for being *Unskilled* is -4, reducing your to-hit bonus
to +35.

A to-hit bonus of +35 is enough to auto-hit AC -15.  The only things
you will ever meet that have AC -15 are particularly fortunate
armour-wearing monsters. (The lowest base AC in the game belongs to
disenchanters and Master Kaen, who have AC -10.  Demogorgon and Rodney
have AC -8.)

Nethack *might* benefit here from monsters that could inflict temporary
debuffs on the player, or from the effects of luck and level being
toned down slightly.

>Rodney gains a level every time he comes back to life.  At one
>point the level he came back to was one more than the level
>he died at.  So using the Staff on him would wear him down
>even in later appearances.  I haven't checked recently if this is
>still true.

It is certainly not true in 3.4.1 (the source version that happens to be
immediately to hand); the wizard's level is always equal to his base
level, plus his total deaths this game, subject to a hard cap of level 49.

>I know level drain doesn't work on demons or riders
>so it matters less as you get deeper, but when it works on a
>monster as nasty as Rodney it's not to be ignored.
